{
  "cleanUrls": true,
  "trailingSlash": false,
  "headers": [
    {
      "source": "/sitemap.xml",
      "headers": [
        { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/xml" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "/robots.txt",
      "headers": [
        { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/plain" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Click **"Commit changes"** → commit directly to `main`.

---

### Step 2 — Vercel Auto-Deploys
Since your GitHub is connected to Vercel, pushing to `main` triggers an automatic deploy. Watch the **Deployments** tab — it'll go green in ~30 seconds.

---

### Step 3 — Verify Both URLs Work
Open these in your browser after deploy:

- `https://lumrexai.com/robots.txt` → should show the robots content
- `https://lumrexai.com/sitemap.xml` → should show the XML content

---

### Step 4 — Submit Sitemap to Google Search Console
Once `https://lumrexai.com/sitemap.xml` is confirmed working:

1. Go to **search.google.com/search-console**
2. Left menu → **Sitemaps**
3. Enter `sitemap.xml` in the box → click **Submit**
4. Status should turn green ✅

---

### Step 5 — Submit to Bing Too
1. Go to **bing.com/webmasters** → verify your site (DNS TXT, same as Google)
2. Submit `https://lumrexai.com/sitemap.xml`
3. Covers Yahoo + DuckDuckGo automatically ✅

---

